IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`
IMPORT `ccc26-principles`

-- ccc26-tests-principles.l4 -- tests for ccc26-principles.l4 (sections 718 to 718.21). Every expected value is written from the text (lines 15190-15250) before the run.

§ `s 718: the objectives (a) to (f); a sanction with one or more of them`

#ASSERT `s 718 the sanction has one or more of the objectives the section lists` (LIST `s 718(a) denunciation of unlawful conduct and of the harm done to victims or to the community`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718 the sanction has one or more of the objectives the section lists` (LIST `s 718(d) rehabilitation of offenders`, `s 718(e) reparations for harm done to victims or to the community`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no objective at all: the section does not say such a sanction is not just, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 718 the sanction has one or more of the objectives the section lists` (LIST) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 718.01: abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years`

#ASSERT `s 718.01 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.01 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the objectives the sections give primary consideration to are (a) denunciation and (b) deterrence
#ASSERT `s 718.01 the objectives given primary consideration` EQUALS LIST `s 718(a) denunciation of unlawful conduct and of the harm done to victims or to the community`, `s 718(b) deterrence of the offender and of other persons`

§ `s 718.02: offences under subsection 270(1), section 270.01 or 270.02 or paragraph 423.1(1)(b)`

#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 270, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 270.01, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 270.02, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 423.1, "(1)(b)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 270(2) and 423.1(1)(a) are not named; neither is section 271
#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 270, "(2)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 423.1, "(1)(a)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 271, "") EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.03: an offence under subsection 445.01(1)`

#ASSERT `s 718.03 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 445.01, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.03 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 445.01, "(2)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.03 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 445, "(1)") EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.04: abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances`

#ASSERT `s 718.04 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.04 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.05: a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3)`

#ASSERT `s 718.05 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 333.1, "(3)") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a first offence is not "second or subsequent"
#ASSERT `s 718.05 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 333.1, "(3)") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.05 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 333.1, "(1)") TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.05 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 348, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.06: a second or subsequent offence under section 348`

#ASSERT `s 718.06 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 348, "(1)") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.06 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 348, "(1)") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.06 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 349, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.07: an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`

#ASSERT `s 718.07 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.07 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.07 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.07 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.1: a sentence must be proportionate to the gravity of the offence and the degree of responsibility of the offender`

#ASSERT `s 718.1 the sentence is proportionate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.1 the sentence is proportionate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.1 the sentence is proportionate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.1 the sentence is proportionate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.2 lead-in: a court that imposes a sentence shall also take into consideration the following principles`

#ASSERT `s 718.2 requires the court to take the principles into consideration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2 requires the court to take the principles into consideration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 718.2(a): the circumstances that shall be deemed to be aggravating`

#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(i) the offence was motivated by bias, prejudice or hate based on race, national or ethnic origin, language, colour, religion, sex, age, mental or physical disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other similar factor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(ii) the offender abused the offender's intimate partner or a member of the victim's or the offender's family` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(ii.1) the offender abused a person under the age of eighteen years` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(ii.2) the offender counselled or otherwise involved a person under the age of 18 years in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(iii) the offender abused a position of trust or authority in relation to the victim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(iii.1) the offence had a significant impact on the victim, considering their age and other personal circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(iii.2) the offence was committed against a person providing health services or services as a first responder in the performance of their duties` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(iv) the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(v) the offence was a terrorism offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(vi) the offence was committed while the offender was subject to a conditional sentence order or released on parole, statutory release or unescorted temporary absence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a)(vii) the commission of the offence had the effect of impeding another person from obtaining health services` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "without limiting the generality of the foregoing": another circumstance is neither deemed aggravating nor deemed not aggravating
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` `s 718.2(a) another circumstance relating to the offence or the offender` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 718.2(a)(viii): violence, threats or attempts of violence and a conviction within the previous five years`

-- sentence imposed on 1 March 2027; the five years run back to 1 March 2022
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` TRUE TRUE (Date 2 3 2022) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` TRUE TRUE (Date 28 2 2022) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a conviction after the day of sentence is not "previous"
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` TRUE TRUE (Date 2 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no previous conviction, or no violence in this offence
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a)(viii) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.2(a): a sentence should be increased or reduced for any relevant aggravating or mitigating circumstances`

#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the sentence should be increased` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the sentence should be increased` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the sentence should be reduced` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(a) the sentence should be reduced` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 718.2(b): a sentence should be similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances`

#ASSERT `s 718.2(b) the sentence meets the principle of parity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(b) the sentence meets the principle of parity` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.2(c): where consecutive sentences are imposed, the combined sentence should not be unduly long or harsh`

#ASSERT `s 718.2(c) the combined sentence is barred as unduly long or harsh` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(c) the combined sentence is barred as unduly long or harsh` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no consecutive sentences: the "where" gate fails
#ASSERT `s 718.2(c) the combined sentence is barred as unduly long or harsh` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(c) the combined sentence is barred as unduly long or harsh` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.2(d): an offender should not be deprived of liberty, if less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances`

#ASSERT `s 718.2(d) deprivation of liberty is barred` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(d) deprivation of liberty is barred` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 718.2(e): all available sanctions, other than imprisonment, that are reasonable and consistent with the harm done should be considered`

--                                                           available, imprisonment, reasonable, consistent with the harm
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) particular attention is due to the circumstances of the offender` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.2(e) particular attention is due to the circumstances of the offender` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 718.201: the abuse of an intimate partner; the increased vulnerability of female victims`

#ASSERT `s 718.201 requires the court to consider the increased vulnerability of female victims` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.201 requires the court to consider the increased vulnerability of female victims` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.201 particular attention is due to the circumstances of the victim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.201 particular attention is due to the circumstances of the victim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 718.201 particular attention is due to the circumstances of the victim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 718.21: a court that imposes a sentence on an organization shall also take into consideration the following factors`

#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(a) any advantage realized by the organization as a result of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(b) the degree of planning involved in carrying out the offence and the duration and complexity of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(c) whether the organization has attempted to conceal its assets, or convert them, in order to show that it is not able to pay a fine or make restitution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(d) the impact that the sentence would have on the economic viability of the organization and the continued employment of its employees` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(e) the cost to public authorities of the investigation and prosecution of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(f) any regulatory penalty imposed on the organization or one of its representatives in respect of the conduct that formed the basis of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(g) whether the organization, or any of its representatives who were involved in the commission of the offence, were convicted of a similar offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body for similar conduct` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(h) any penalty imposed by the organization on a representative for their role in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(i) any restitution that the organization is ordered to make or any amount that the organization has paid to a victim of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21(j) any measures that the organization has taken to reduce the likelihood of it committing a subsequent offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "the following factors": a factor the text does not list is not covered
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` TRUE `s 718.21 another factor` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not an organization: the relative clause "A court that imposes a sentence on an organization" is not met
#ASSERT `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` FALSE `s 718.21(a) any advantage realized by the organization as a result of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING
